// std.sea -- the Sea prelude (docs/DESIGN.md 2.5, LANGUAGE.md section 10).
//
// The driver streams this file to pass 1 ahead of every program, and pass 2b drops each
// function the program does not reach. It will hold the library functions that are naturally
// written in Sea with value semantics, marked (P) in LANGUAGE.md section 10: linspace,
// meshgrid, setdiff and bincount.
//
// Those functions need arrays, which arrive in phase 4 (DESIGN.md section 8). Until then this
// file holds comments only; the driver still streams it, so the prelude path is exercised
// on every compilation.
